  "final_answer": "If the backend endpoint **`POST /api/agent`** is deleted, it will introduce a **BREAKING** change in the Angular frontend. \n\nThe following TypeScript consumers, services, and UI components rely directly on this endpoint via `AgentService.saveAgent()` and would be broken:\n\n### 1. Service Layer Consumers\n* **`AgentService`** (`ui-ngx/src/app/core/http/agent.service.ts`)\n  * **Method:** `saveAgent(agent: Agent, entityGroupIds?: string | string[], config?: RequestConfig)`\n  * **Impact:** This is the core HTTP wrapper method that constructs and executes the `POST` request to `/api/agent` (with optional query parameters `?entityGroupIds=...`).\n* **`EntityService`** (`ui-ngx/src/app/core/http/entity.service.ts`)\n  * **Method:** `saveGroupEntityObservable(entity: BaseData<EntityId>, entityGroupIds: string | string[], config?: RequestConfig)`\n  * **Impact:** Within the `EntityType.AGENT` case of the switch statement, it delegates to `this.agentService.saveAgent()`.\n\n### 2. UI and Dialog/Configuration Consumers\n* **`AgentCreateDialogService`** (`ui-ngx/src/app/modules/home/pages/agent/agent-create-dialog.service.ts`)\n  * **Method:** `create()`\n  * **Impact:** The `saveEntity` callback of the `EntityTableConfig` object calls `this.agentService.saveAgent(agent)`, meaning creating a new Agent via the creation dialog would fail.\n* **`AgentGroupConfig`** (`ui-ngx/src/app/modules/home/pages/agent/agent-group-config.factory.ts`)\n  * **Impact:** In the group configuration setup, `config.saveEntity` is assigned to `agent => this.agentService.saveAgent(agent)`.\n* **`AgentsTableConfigResolver`** (`ui-ngx/src/app/modules/home/pages/agent/agents-table-config.resolver.ts`)\n  * **Impact:** Within the entity table config resolution, `config.saveEntity`",
